cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use ChampHLA, please cite the software and the accompanying paper.
title: ChampHLA analysis, audit and manuscript code
abstract: >-
  The analysis, audit and freeze code accompanying the ChampHLA benchmark of
  equal-weight caller consensus for short-read HLA class-I typing. This repository
  holds the statistical evaluation, the claim auditor that ties every reported value
  to a result registry, the provenance freeze manifests, and the manuscript sources.
  The Nextflow DSL2 workflow that runs the callers and harmonises their output is a
  separate repository, https://github.com/uoozcan/ChampHLA; every path cited in the
  manuscript resolves inside this repository rather than that one.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/uoozcan/ChampHLA-paper"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
# date-released is deliberately absent rather than carrying a placeholder. CFF 1.2.0
# types it as a date, so "TO CONFIRM" made this file fail schema validation, which
# broke GitHub's citation widget and Zenodo ingestion. It is optional in 1.2.0, so
# omitting it keeps the file valid. Add it, with the DOI below, when the release tag
# is cut. It remains an outstanding author field: see AUTHOR_FIELDS_TO_COMPLETE.md.
#
# At release, add the archived DOI as:
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#       description: Archived release of this repository
keywords:
  - HLA typing
  - consensus methods
  - ensemble benchmarking
  - immunogenomics
  - reproducible workflows
